A||||8||Kasdan||Motor Swap Help-2 days!||||1||
Z||000000||Kasdan||09-27-2001||10:49 PM||||Im having a new longblock devivered to my house in 2 days, and i will be installing it myself.  i need all the help you guys can give me (tranny, heads, intake, ignition, accessories, etc)  i need specific Step-by-step instructions on how to swap a 2.8 auto with a new motor.  im not changing tannys or anything, just the motor (throw rod)<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">         <BR>Power Steering, Holley Scoop<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000001||Leadfoot||09-27-2001||11:32 PM||||The swap is straigh forward.  Just yank out your old engine.  Strip it down and clean the parts (make sure you know exactly where each bolt goes).  Once they are clean, paint them and put them on.  You should be able to install everything on your new engine before it goes in like the exhaust system, wiring harnesses, and manifolds.  If I were you I would order the saturn exhaust manifold studs and nuts.  I don't remember the part #s but they are on the forum.  Doing this will save you from having to replace the bolts while the engine is in the car.  Also, when it comes to connecting the fuel supply and return line to the fuel rail manifold be very careful not to cross thread the fitting.  As a final note, I would recommend you order the valve cover gaskets, intake manifold gaskets (both from the fierostore) and the cold start o-ring gasket kit (from carparts.com P#17111954).  The gasket kit that came with the long block was missing these items.  If you need more help just email me.  Good luck!  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||09-28-2001||01:13 AM||||sorry for getting off topic here but what happens if we "don't remember where everybolt goes"...who here can tell me where they go?  because I"m doing a complete rebuild on my 2.8...thx.<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||09-28-2001||02:04 AM||||If you don't remember you're SOL!  Well, maybe.<P>Get some cardboard and draw the part you are removing bolts from on it. Punch some holes and put the bolts through it where they go.  Or just put the bolts through the removed part and put a masking tape flag on the thread(clean before install).<P>Good luck!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Kasdan||09-28-2001||08:43 AM||||Is there an online guide on how to do it the most straightforward and simple way possible?<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">         <BR>Power Steering, Holley Scoop<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000005||mshill||09-28-2001||09:27 AM||||Better yet, do what I did and video tape (up close and personal) every major step of the disassembly.  I also got into the habit of putting nuts and bolts into clear platic bags and marking what they were from.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||thomas_l||09-28-2001||10:17 AM||||After having to install a trans when I first got mine, I would set the cradle on some short stands or wood blocks, unhook everything, and lift the body as high as possible or completely off if you can.<P>As far as remembering where stuff goes - try to keep like parts/fasteners together (i.e. putting valve cover bolts inside the covers when you set them aside). It's not 100% perfect, but way faster than sorting things into labeled baggies or boxes.<p>[This message has been edited by thomas_l (edited 09-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||SLYGUY||09-28-2001||01:27 PM||||I have a pair of manuals that, between the two, cover just about everything you would need to know when removing/installing an engine. Check them out<P>Haynes Fiero (1st choice)<BR>Chiltons'    (2nd choice)<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000008||thomas_l||10-01-2001||09:25 AM||||You get it done?||||reg||5
